The next morning, Arin packed a lantern and followed the map. Deep in the forest, he found an abandoned tower wrapped in vines. At the top of the tower stood a massive clock frozen at midnight.

As he examined it, he noticed one missing gear.

The silver pocket watch.

Arin placed the watch into the empty space. Instantly, the giant clock roared to life. Bells echoed across the forest, and thousands of glowing fireflies burst into the sky like stars waking up.

An old voice whispered behind him.

“You restored the Keeper’s Clock.”

A woman in a blue cloak appeared from the shadows. She explained that the tower once protected the village by keeping balance between time and nature. When the clock stopped, the forest slowly began to fade.

As the gears turned again, flowers bloomed around the tower walls, rivers sparkled brighter, and the cold air softened.
